[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558237739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2558237739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2558237739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ye5wr","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T20:51:13Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T20:51:13Z","body":"Copied from the issue:\r\n\r\nin `void ItemList::gui_input(const Ref<InputEvent> &p_event)`\r\n\r\nwe detect what item is clicked by\r\n\r\n`int closest = get_item_at_position(mb->get_position(), true);`\r\n\r\nBut then on line `emit_signal(SNAME(\"multi_selected\"), i, true);`\r\n\r\nWe emit a signal, and in the project with the error the signal handler for this clears items\r\n\r\nSo we then\r\n\r\n`if (items[i].selectable && select_mode == SELECT_TOGGLE) {`\r\n\r\nWhich is where the crash happens, at this point the closest value is still set to 1, or 2, but items has been cleared.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558237739/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558248777","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2558248777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2558248777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ye8dJ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T21:46:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T21:46:48Z","body":"What PR caused the regression? It's easier to assess the fix in context of what made it necessary.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558248777/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558270600","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2558270600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2558270600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YfByI","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T23:48:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T23:48:37Z","body":"> What PR caused the regression? It's easier to assess the fix in context of what made it necessary.\r\n\r\nI will find the pr, and link it again tomorrow, but basically what it did was add this extra if block after the signal. Prior to the pr there was no extra check, so we were not crashing, but sending a bogus index in the signal.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558270600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558425775","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2558425775","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2558425775,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yfnqv","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-22T11:39:08Z","updated_at":"2024-12-22T11:39:08Z","body":"The regression was caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99355 notice how there is a second conditional after the signal fired that was previously not there.\r\n\r\nAlso notice that without that secondary if block, the data in the second signal was garbage. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558425775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558592925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2558592925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2558592925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YgQed","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-22T20:43:43Z","updated_at":"2024-12-22T20:43:43Z","body":"CC @havi05 @KoBeWi ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558592925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558954389","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2558954389","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2558954389,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YhouV","user":{"login":"havi05","id":71942164,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTQyMTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71942164?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05","html_url":"https://github.com/havi05","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/havi05/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T05:47:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T06:57:35Z","body":"I tried to reproduce the error, but wasn't able to do so. (Does this only appear on the mono version?) Clearing all Items when the `multi_selected` signal fired didn't cause any errors on my side. (using 4.4dev7)\r\n\r\n~~I also don't understand how the first if-condition in [line 749](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714/files?diff=unified&w=0#diff-8cbdaea96117950192d3baac12f8cff87b2c4598e04e5df1aae4758f5de3b09bR749) can modifiy the list of Items, because it checks if `select_mode != SELECT_TOGGLE` is true and the second (new) one ([line 770](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714/files?diff=unified&w=0#diff-8cbdaea96117950192d3baac12f8cff87b2c4598e04e5df1aae4758f5de3b09bR770)) checks the opposite.~~\r\n\r\nEdit: I understand now where the issue is appearing. (The first check in line 770 is problematic. ) I think I would prefer to solve it this way:\r\n```\r\nif (select_mode == SELECT_SINGLE) {\r\n\tif (items[i].selectable && (!items[i].selected || allow_reselect)) {\r\n\t\tselect(i, select_mode == SELECT_SINGLE || !mb->is_command_or_control_pressed());\r\n\t\temit_signal(SceneStringName(item_selected), i);\r\n\r\n} else if (select_mode == SELECT_TOGGLE) {\r\n\tif (items[i].selectable) {\r\n\t\tif (items[i].selected) {\r\n\t\t\tdeselect(i);\r\n\t\t\tcurrent = i;\r\n\t\t\temit_signal(SNAME(\"multi_selected\"), i, false);\r\n\r\n\t\t} else {\r\n\t\t\tselect(i, false);\r\n\t\t\tcurrent = i;\r\n\t\t\temit_signal(SNAME(\"multi_selected\"), i, true);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n} else {\r\n\temit_signal(SNAME(\"multi_selected\"), i, true);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nPersonally I think this would be better readable than a return mid function. What do you think? \r\n\r\n_Since I'm on vacation it is difficult for me to debug this, but I will try my best to help you._","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558954389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559692414","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2559692414","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2559692414,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ykc5-","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T13:15:06Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T13:16:08Z","body":"@havi05 Sure I can do that too, I think generally we prefer early exits in Godot, that's why it is like this. But I can make it an if/then branch also. \r\n\r\n@KoBeWi @akien-mga any preferences? \r\n\r\nNote also that it doesn't solve the pre-existing problem of `emit_signal(SNAME(\"item_clicked\"), i, get_local_mouse_position(), mb->get_button_index());` being garbage if the new signal changes the ItemList. So we still need the code I wrote before that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2559692414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560316525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2560316525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2560316525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ym1Rt","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T21:28:44Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T21:29:17Z","body":"tbh the crash can be fixed by just inverting the condition:\r\n\r\n`if select_mode == SELECT_TOGGLE && items[i].selectable`\r\n\r\nThe code currently checks for the opposite thing independently, i.e.\r\n`(items[i].selectable && (!items[i].selected || allow_reselect) && select_mode != SELECT_TOGGLE)\r\n`items[i].selectable && select_mode == SELECT_TOGGLE`\r\nthese 2 lines are mutually exclusive, because the mode is either SELECT_TOGGLE or not, so this begs to add an `else` somewhere.\r\n\r\nOr just use the code from havi, it looks cleaner.\r\n\r\nAlso I'd avoid calling `get_item_at_position()` just in case the user messed the list; it's unnecessary calculation. If the index can be invalidated, just do `ERR_FAIL_INDEX(i, items.size())` with a message that modifying list in signal callback is not supported and you should use a deferred call.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560316525/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560423357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2560423357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2560423357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YnPW9","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-23T23:23:12Z","updated_at":"2024-12-23T23:23:21Z","body":"If we don't want to support people changing the selection mode etc from inside the handler then this can be done differently, sure. I will make a revision. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560423357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571460302","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100714#issuecomment-2571460302","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100714","id":2571460302,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZRV7O","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-05T01:12:25Z","updated_at":"2025-01-05T01:12:25Z","body":"@KoBeWi pretty sure this is fixed properly now.","author_association":"MEMBE